From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:42:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: check the length of the ACPI battery information
 package

nv_acpi_find_battery_info() indexed the _BIX or _BIF package without checking
its length, so a short package was read past the end of the object. Treat it
like any other invalid battery information.

Builds against 7.3 and boots; the failure path hasn't been run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
index 1a7913ae..99c0536b 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
@@ -1557,6 +1557,13 @@ static acpi_status nv_acpi_find_battery_info(
         battery_technology_offset = BIF_BATTERY_TECHNOLOGY_OFFSET;
     }
 
+    if (object_package->package.count <= battery_technology_offset)
+    {
+        nv_printf(NV_DBG_INFO, "NVRM: Battery method output is too short\n");
+        kfree(buf.pointer);
+        return AE_OK;
+    }
+
     /*
      * Only checking here for Battery technology type.
      * Other fields like Battery Model/Serial number could also be checked but
